{"name":"Vixen","hex":"#573d37","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Vixen","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["The fourth reindeer of Santa Claus."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Vixen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vixen (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Vixen is an American all-female glam metal band formed in Saint Paul, Minnesota, in 1973. During its most commercially successful period from 1987 to 1992, the band consisted of Jan Kuehnemund, Janet Gardner, Share Ross, and Roxy Petrucci (drums)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Vixen_Band.jpg/330px-Vixen_Band.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vixen_(band)","wikidata":"Q1865430"},{"title":"Vixen (character)","blocks":[{"text":"Vixen is a superheroine appearing in American comic books published by DC Comics. Created by Gerry Conway and Bob Oksner, she first appeared in Action Comics #521, in a Superman story, working alongside the superhero to catch a poacher. An African superhero, she is considered one of the earliest created black superheroes in comics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Vixen_%28DC_Comics_character%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vixen_(character)","wikidata":"Q2736581"},{"title":"Fox","blocks":[{"text":"Foxes are small-to-medium-sized omnivorous mammals belonging to several genera of the family Canidae. They have a flattened skull; upright, triangular ears; a pointed, slightly upturned snout; and a long, bushy tail (\"brush\")."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg/330px-Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox","wikidata":"Q8331"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia